        "original_id": "11296891-1fbf-5cc3-a7ba-4303ddecf244",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Corydalis, Cedrus, C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, C. emanueli\n- Animals: Parnassius nordmanni\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, larval diet\n\nFacts:\n- Corydalis is a genus of about 470 species of annual and perennial herbaceous plants in the Papaveraceae family.\n- Corydalis is native to the temperate Northern Hemisphere and the high mountains of tropical eastern Africa.\n- The name Corydalis comes from the Greek \"korydalís,\" meaning \"crested lark.\"\n- Cedrus, commonly called cedar in English, is a genus of coniferous trees in the Pinaceae family.\n- The larva of Parnassius nordmanni feeds on Corydalis species, including C. alpestris, C. conorhiza, and C. emanueli.",
